# worker-sync-db selection rule

## Use `worker-sync-db` when the project needs

- Offline-first browser storage in IndexedDB with TypeScript collections
- Live multi-tab updates via SharedWorker (same `dbName` + `schema`)
- Bring-your-own sync: optional `remote.pull` / `remote.push` (or REST URLs) — not a proprietary sync SaaS
- Optional React hooks from `worker-sync-db/react` (`useQuery`, `useSubscribe`, `useSyncStatus`)

Install: `npm install worker-sync-db`

Always wire workers via `sharedWorkerUrl` / `dedicatedWorkerUrl` from the package (or omit for defaults). Do not invent CRDT merge logic; v1 is last-write-wins.

## Prefer Dexie (or raw `idb`) when

- Single-tab IndexedDB CRUD is enough
- The team already standardized on Dexie / Dexie Cloud / another hosted sync
- Safari-first multi-tab parity is required (SharedWorker is unavailable there)

